          ":question/problem": "$\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[(2{t}^{2}+3)^{2}]=\\,$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}",
          ":question/worked-solution": "First, let's define a function $h(t):$\n\n$$\nh(t)=(2{t}^{2}+3)^{2}\n$$\n\nTo differentiate this function, we use the chain rule. Let \n\n$$\ng(t)=2{t}^{2}+3,\\,h(g(t))=g(t)^{2}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating our functions, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{\u2032}(t) & =(2{t}^{2}+3)^{\u2032}=4t, \\\\ {h}^{\u2032}(g(t)) & =({g}^{2})^{\u2032}=2g.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[(2{t}^{2}+3)^{2}] & ={h}^{\u2032}(t) \\\\  & ={h}^{\u2032}(g(t))\\cdot {g}^{\u2032}(t) \\\\  & =2g\\cdot 4t \\\\  & =8t(2{t}^{2}+3).\\end{aligned}\n$$"
